 <text type="manuscript">
  <body>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf001r" facs="uva.00148.001.jpg" type="recto"/>
   <note hand="#h04" place="top" type="authorial">Please keep Copy as perfect as possible <hi rend="Underline">and return</hi></note>
   <note hand="#h03" place="top" rend="circled" type="authorial">follow copy in punctuation, capitalization &amp;c</note>
   <note hand="#h04" place="top" rend="circled" type="authorial">55c</note>
   <note hand="#h02" place="top" type="authorial">75lead</note>
   <note hand="#h04" place="top" rend="circled" type="authorial">Syndicate</note>
   <addSpan spanTo="#a015" hand="#h04" rend="circled"/><metamark function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02" rend="highlight">lead all</hi></metamark><anchor xml:id="a015"/>
   <head type="main" rend="Underline">How I made a book <unclear reason="illegible" cert="low"
    resp="#ja">,</unclear> or tried to.</head>
   <byline>By Walt Whitman</byline>
   <addSpan spanTo="#a013"/><metamark target="#a001" function="add">&#8248; &#8248;</metamark><anchor xml:id="a013"/><addSpan place="top" xml:id="a001" spanTo="#a012"/><ab>(<hi rend="Underline">Copyright 1885</hi>)</ab><anchor xml:id="a012"/>
  <div type="section">
   <addSpan spanTo="#a014" hand="#h04"/><head type="sub" rend="doubleUnderline">I</head><anchor xml:id="a014"/>
   <p>My friends have more
    than once suggested&#8212;<subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">(the</del><add seq="2"><metamark target="#a002" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a002" seq="3">&#8212;(or may-be</add></subst>
    <add><metamark target="#a003" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a003">the</add> garrulity of advancing age <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">seems</del><add seq="2"><metamark target="#a004 #a005" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><del seq="4"><add xml:id="a004" place="above" seq="3">has</add></del><del seq="6"><add place="above" xml:id="a005" seq="5">is</add></del></subst>
    <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">indeed</del><add place="above" seq="2">is</add></subst> pos<del hand="#h04">s</del>ess<restore rend="erasure"><del rend="overstrike">ing</del></restore><del rend="erasure"><add place="below"><metamark target="#a006" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a006">ed</add></del> me,<del rend="overstrike">!</del>)&#8212;some
   embryonic facts of "Leaves of
   Grass," and how I entered
   upon them. Dr. Bucke has
   already <add hand="#h01"><metamark target="#a007" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a007">fully and fairly</add> described the preparation
   of my poetic field,
   with the particular ad general
   ploughing, planting,
   seeding and occupation of the
   ground till everything was
   fertilized, rooted, and ready</p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf001v" facs="uva.00148.002.jpg" type="verso"/>
   <p>to start its own way, for
   good or bad. Not until <del rend="overstrike">all</del>
   after this was all settled
   did I begin any definite
   and serious acquaintance, or
   attempt at acquaintance with
   poetic literature. Along in
   my 16th year I had become
   possessor of a stout <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">well&#11840;cramm'd</del><add place="above" seq="2">well&#11840;crammed</add></subst>
   <add place="below"><metamark target="#a008" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a008">1000 page</add> octavo volume. (I have it yet)
   containing Walter Scott's Poetry
   entire <metamark function="link" xml:id="e001">*</metamark><add rend="circled"><metamark function="emphasize" target="#e001"><hi hand="#h02">note a</hi></metamark></add>&#8212;an inexhaustable mine
   and treasury of poetic study, (especially
   the endless forests and
   jungles of notes)&#8212;has been so to
   me for fifty years, and remains
   so to this day.</p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf002r" facs="uva.00148.003.jpg" type="recto"/>
   <p><note hand="#h02" place="top">76</note><add>&#182;</add><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">Years</del> <del rend="overwrite" hand="#h04">l</del><add hand="#h04">L</add>ater, <add place="below"><metamark target="#a017" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a017">at intervals,</add> I used to
   go off, <del rend="overstrike">at intervals</del>, sometimes
   for a week at a stretch,
   down in the dountry, or to
   Long Island's sea-shores;<metamark function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02">lead</hi></metamark>&#8212;there,
   in the presence of <del hand="#h04" rend="overstrike">natural
   and</del> outdoor influences. I went
   over thoroughly the Old and
   New Testaments and absorbed
   (probably to better advantage for
   me than in any library or
   indoor room&#8212;it makes such
   difference <hi rend="underline">where</hi> you read,)
   Shakspere, Ossian, the best</p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf002v" facs="uva.00148.004.jpg" type="verso"/>
   <p><addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a018"/>versions I could get of Homer,
   Eschylus, Sophocles, the old<anchor xml:id="a018"/>
   German <unclear reason="illegible"
    cert="high" resp="#ja">Nibelungen</unclear> the ancient
   Hindoo poems, and one or two
   other masterpieces, Dante's among
   them. As it happened, I read
   the latter mostly in an old
   wood. The Iliad, (Buckley's
   prose version) I read first
   thoroughly on the peninsula
   of Orient northeast end of<add hand="#h02"><metamark function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add></p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf003r" facs="uva.00148.005.jpg" type="recto"/>
   <p><add hand="#h02"><metamark function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add>Long Island, in a sheltered
   hollow of rocks and sand,
   with the sea on each side.
   I have<addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a019"/>
    wonder'd since <metamark function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02">lead</hi></metamark>
   why I was not overwhelm'd
   by those mighty-masters.
   Likely, because I read them, <note hand="#h02" place="margin">76</note>
   as described, in the full presence
   of Nature, under the sun,
   with the far-spreading landscape
   and vistas or the sea <retrace cause="emphasize" hand="#h01"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">surf</del></retrace>
   rolling in. <add place="below" hand="#h04"><metamark target="#a020" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><retrace rend="overstrike" cause="emphasize" hand="#h01"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"><add place="above" hand="#h04" xml:id="a020">Giving myself many intervals</add></del></retrace> I <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">read</del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark target="#a021" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a021" seq="3">absorbed</add></subst> very
   <del rend="overstrike"><unclear cert="high" resp="#ja">lie</unclear></del> leisurely, <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04"><add place="above" hand="#h04"><unclear cert="low" resp="#ja">giving m</unclear></add></del> following the
   mood. <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">(</del>May I not say that
   in me, there, those <del rend="overstrike">old</del><retrace rend="overstrike" hand="#h01" cause="emphasize"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04"><add place="above">antique</add></del></retrace> <retrace hand="#h01"><add place="above" hand="#h04">works</add></retrace><add place="above">old</add> <del rend="overstrike">maestros</del>
   certainly had <hi rend="underline">one</hi> <add place="below"><metamark target="#a022" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a022">fully</add> appreciative
    <add place="above">and exultant</add> modern <retrace rend="overstrike" cause="emphasize" hand="#h01"><retrace rend="overstrike" cause="emphasize" hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">listener</del></retrace></retrace><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h01"><add place="above" hand="#h04"><retrace hand="#h02" cause="illegible">a</retrace>bsorber</add></del><del hand="#h02"><add place="below" hand="#h02">peruser?</add></del><add place="below" hand="#h01">peruser?</add>?<del rend="overstrike">)</del>.... <add place="above" hand="#h03" rend="circled"><metamark function="adjust">run in</metamark></add>Returning
   to New York I alternated with
   <del rend="overstrike">the musical</del> <del hand="#h02">absorptions</del><add place="above" hand="#h01">the</add><add place="above" hand="#h02">attendances</add>
   mention'd <add place="below" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a023" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h04" xml:id="a023"><retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize">by Dr. Bucke</retrace> <retrace rend="overstrike" hand="#h01"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">in the <retrace rend="overstrike" hand="#h03" cause="emphasize">memoranda</retrace></del></retrace></add> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">by <retrace hand="#h03" rend="overstrike" cause="emphasize">Dr.</retrace> B.</del> especially
   <del rend="overstrike">with</del> the singing of <add place="below"><metamark target="#a024" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a024">the contralto</add> Alboni<anchor xml:id="a019"/>
    <addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a025"/>
    and the Italian <gap reason="illegible" extent="one character"/> opera generally.
    <del rend="overstrike">...</del>All this and these, <retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">I sang</del></retrace>,
    saturating and imbuing everything
    before I touch'd pen
    to paper <handShift/> <gap extent="one character" reason="illegible"></gap> on my own account<del rend="overstrike"><gap extent="punctuation" reason="illegible"/></del><add>&#182;</add><anchor xml:id="a025"/></p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf003v" facs="uva.00148.006.jpg" type="verso"/>
   <p><milestone unit="glued"/><add>&#182;</add>Towards the last I had
   <add place="below"><metamark target="#a026" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a026" hand="#h04">among much else</add>look'd over Edgar Poe's <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04"><add hand="#h04" place="above">earlier</add></del> poems&#8212;
   <add place="below" rend="marked" hand="#h04"><metamark target="#a027" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a027" hand="#h04">of whom</add> was not an admirer tho' I
   always saw that <retrace cause="emphasize" hand="#h01"><del hand="#h02">besides</del></retrace><add place="above" hand="#h02">beyond</add> their
   <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">inimitable</del> <del hand="#h04" rend="overstrike">though</del><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h01"><add place="above" hand="#h04">yet</add></del> limited range
   of <del rend="overstrike">sweet</del> melody, (like perpetual
   chimes of music bells, ringing
   from lower <hi rend="underline">b</hi> flat up to <hi rend="underline">g</hi>.)
   They were expressions, and perhaps
   never excell'd ones, of
   certain <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">extravagant</del><add place="above" seq="2">pronounced</add></subst> phases of
   human morbidity. (The
   Poetic area is very <del rend="overstrike">very</del> spacious
    &#8212;has <add place="below" hand="#h03"><metamark target="#a028" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a028" hand="#h04">so</add> many mansions!)
   But I was repaid in Poe's prose
   by the idea that <add place="below" hand="#h01" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a029" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a029" hand="#h02">(at any rate for our occasions <add place="below" hand="#h04"><metamark target="#a030" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a030" hand="#h04">and</add> our day)</add> there can be
    no such thing, <add place="below" hand="#h04"><metamark target="#a031" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a031" hand="#h04"><retrace hand="#h01"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">at any rate</del></retrace> for <retrace cause="emphasize" hand="#h01"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02"><add hand="#h01" place="above">contemporary</add></del></retrace></add> <retrace cause="emphasize" hand="#h04"><del rend="overstrike">for</del></retrace> <del rend="overstrike">modern purposes</del>,
   as a <hi rend="Underline">long</hi> poem. The
   same thought had been haunting
   my mind before, but P's argument,
   though short, work'd the sum
   out, and proved it to me.</p>
   <metamark function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02">78lead</hi></metamark>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf004r" facs="uva.00148.007.jpg" type="recto"/>
   <note hand="#h03" place="top" type="editorial"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">5</del></note>
   <metamark function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02">79lead</hi></metamark>
   <p><addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a036"/><add hand="#h03">&#182;</add>Another <del rend="overstrike">point</del> point had an
   early settlement, <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04">which</del> clear<subst><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04" seq="1">'d</del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark target="#a032" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h04" xml:id="a032" seq="3">ing</add></subst>
   the ground greatly. I saw from
   the time my enterprise and
   questionings <add place="below"><metamark target="#a033" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a033">positively shaped themselves.</add> (how best can I
   express my own <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">days</del><add place="above" seq="2">era</add></subst> and surroundings,
   America, Democracy?) <del rend="overstrike">positively
   shaped themselves</del> that the
   trunk and centre whence the
   answer was to radiate, and to
   which all <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">must</del><add place="above" seq="2">should</add></subst> return from <add rend="marked #h03" place="below"><metamark target="#a034" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a034">straying</add>
   however far a distance, <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">should</del><add place="above" seq="2">must</add></subst>
   be an identical body and soul,
   a <hi rend="tripleUnderline">P</hi>ersonality&#8212;which personality,
   after many considerations
   and ponderings I deliberately
   settled should be myself <add place="below"><metamark target="#a035" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a035">&#8212;indeed could not be any other.</add><anchor xml:id="a036"/>
   then the two conflicting forces
   of a character fitted to our
   New World&#8212;not only the free
   and independent "sovereignty
   of one's sellf," but the acknowledge-
   </p>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf004v" facs="uva.00148.008.jpg" type="verso"/>
   <p><addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a037"/>ment of that self as result
   of the past and part of <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">the</del><add place="above" seq="2">its</add></subst>
    whole variform social <add place="below"><metamark target="#a038" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a038">literary</add> and
   political product, with the
   many dominating ties and involvements
   thereof, (from the past,
   from our mothers and father and
   theirs before them) imperatively to
   be considered and allowed for&#8212;<anchor xml:id="a037"/>
   assumed a settled part in
   my scheme. I felt strongly,
   (whether I have shown it, or not.)
   that to the true and full estimate
   of the <del rend="overstrike">pr</del> <hi rend="tripleUnderline">P</hi>resent, both
   the <hi rend="tripleUnderline">P</hi>ast and the <hi rend="tripleUnderline">F</hi>uture are
   main considerations.</p>
   </div>
   
   <pb xml:id="leaf005r" facs="uva.00148.009.jpg" type="recto"/>
   <div type="section">
    <addSpan spanTo="#a039" hand="#h04"/><head type="sub" rend="doubleUnderline">II</head><anchor xml:id="a039"/>
    <metamark place="top" function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02">80</hi></metamark>
    <p><addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a040"/><add>&#182;</add>These, however, and much
    more, might have gone on,
    and come to nought (almost
    positively would have come to
    nought.) if a sudden,<metamark place="above" function="adjust"><hi hand="#h02">lead</hi></metamark> vast,
    terrible, direct and indirect
    stimulus for new and national
    poetic expression, had not
    been given to me. It is certain.<anchor xml:id="a040"/>
     <addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a041"/>I say, that <add place="below"><metamark target="#a042" function="add" rend="marked">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a042">&#8212;although I had made a start before&#8212;</add> only from the
    occurence of the <hi rend="tripleUnderline">S</hi>ecession <hi rend="tripleUnderline">W</hi>ar,
    and what it show'd <metamark><hi hand="#h04">&#8248;</hi></metamark> me as by
    flashes of lightning, with the
    emotional depths it sounded
    and arous'd, (<retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize"><add place="below" hand="#h04"><metamark target="#a043" function="add" rend="marked">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a043">of course</add></retrace> I don't mean in
    my own heart only, I saw it
    just as plainly in others, in
    millions)<add place="above">&#8212;that</add> &#8212;only from the strong
    flare and provocation of <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">its</del><add place="above" seq="2">that war's</add></subst>
    sights and scenes the final
    reason<add hand="#h04">s</add>&#8209;for&#8209;being <add place="below"><metamark target="#a044" function="add" rend="marked">&#8248;</metamark></add><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h04"><add place="above" xml:id="a044">and <unclear reason="illegible" resp="#ja" cert="high">authoritative</unclear> endorsement</add></del> <del rend="overstrike"><add place="above" hand="#h04"><gap reason="illegible" extent="one word"/> at</add></del> of an autoch-</p>
    
    <pb xml:id="leaf005v" facs="uva.00148.010.jpg" type="verso"/>
    <metamark place="top"><hi hand="#h02">81</hi></metamark>
    <note hand="#h03" place="top" type="editorial"><del rend="overstrike" hand="#h02">7</del></note>
    <metamark place="top"><hi hand="#h02">lead</hi></metamark>
    <p><addSpan rend="pasteon" spanTo="#a045"/>
     thonic song definitely <subst><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark target="#a046" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h04" seq="3"><retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize" seq="4">came forth</retrace></add><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">appear'd</del></subst>
     <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h01"><add place="above" hand="#h04"><retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize">and di</retrace>splayed itself</add></del> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h01"><add place="above" hand="#h04"><retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize">themselves</retrace></add></del> <del rend="overstrike" hand="#h01"><add place="above" hand="#h04">itself</add></del> to me. I went down to the war
     field, <retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize"><add place="below" hand="#h04"><metamark target="#a047" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h04" xml:id="a047">in Virginia</add></retrace> (end of 1862,) lived thenceforward
     in camp,&#8212;saw great
     battles, and the days and nights
     afterward&#8212;<del rend="overstrike">partook to the full,
     from the very midst of them</del>,
     all the fluctuations, gloom,
     despair, <add place="below"><metamark target="#a048" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a048">of those times&#8212;</add> hopes again arous'd,
     courage evoked&#8212;death readily
     risk'd&#8212;<hi rend="Underline">the cause</hi> too&#8212;<del rend="overstrike">of</del> <add place="below"><metamark target="#a049" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a049">&#8212;along and filling</add> those
     <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">mighty</del><add place="below" seq="2"><metamark target="#a050" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a050" hand="#h04" seq="3"><retrace hand="#h01" cause="emphasize" seq="4">agonistic</retrace></add></subst>&#8212;and lurid years &#8212;the real
     parturition years (more than 177<gap reason="illegible" unit="chars" extent="1"></gap>-'83)
    <anchor xml:id="a045"/></p>
    
